## Tech Stack

- TypeScript
- Bun

## Workflow Setup

- Always use Bun for adding dependencies
- Differentiate between production and development dependencies using appropriate flags

## Coding Standards

- Write all new code in TypeScript
- Implement proper TypeScript types for all variables, functions, and return values
- Use barrel imports for clean module organization
- Implement comprehensive error handling and input validation

## Best Practices

- Prioritize performance optimization and code readability
- Follow SOLID principles
- Write clean, maintainable code with minimal technical debt

## IMPORTANT!!!

- Verify all files for errors before considering tasks complete
- Run all project tests after implementing changes to ensure functionality

## Tests

- Develop meaningful tests that validate core functionality
- If no useful tests can be written for a particular component, explicitly explain why